body:
Hi,

The quarterly HSE awards are open for nominations, and the window closes on Friday at 12:00. We have one nomination each for the site and [AREA], and I would like us to put forward at least two more before the deadline.

The panel looks for practical examples where someone has gone beyond the basics. Good candidates would be people who have:

- kept their work area clear and safe for the crews following them;
- raised a near miss and helped to close it out with a clear fix;
- set up a permit or lifting plan that made the job safer without slowing it down;
- trained or coached a newer member of the team on a task.

Please send me the name, role and a short description of the action, no more than five lines each. I will then put them through to the customer's panel with [CUST_PM] copied in.

Could you also check whether the scaffold team on the north side has anyone who has shown real improvement since the last quarter. They were not in the last round, and I think they deserve a look.

Thanks,

I am writing to share the outcome of the review into the minor plant collision at [AREA] last week, and the actions we have taken.

A telehandler reversing near the skid frame struck the handrail on the access walkway. No one was injured, and the only damage was a scuffed and bent section of handrail, which has been replaced. The operator was working alone and did not have a banksman in position, and the reverse alarm was not audible over the compressor noise nearby.

The review found three contributing factors:

- the lift route had not been planned against the plant layout drawing;
- the exclusion zone around the skid had been removed to allow a pipe delivery and was not reinstated;
- the operator had not been briefed on the revised walkway layout.

We have taken the following actions:

- a banksman is now required for all reversing movements within 15 metres of process equipment, and this is written into the lifting plan template;
- the exclusion zone is to be reinstated at the end of each delivery, checked by the shift supervisor before work continues;
- all plant operators have been briefed on the revised walkway layout, with the drawing signed as read;
- a rear-view camera is being fitted to the telehandler on hire.

We would be grateful if you could share the summary with [COW] and the other contractors on the site, so the banksman requirement applies to everyone working around the skid area. I will bring the closure record to the next site meeting.
